        "narration": "The morning barge noses into Tallow Docks through a fog that smells of mutton fat and bayberry, and the whole quay is candles: crates of them, carts of them, a chandler's boy asleep on a pallet of beeswax tapers with his mouth open. High on the hill the Everflame burns in the Margrave's palace, pale in the daylight, which is the only time anyone here says it looks small. You step onto the boards with everything you own in one bag. A jackdaw you did not bring lands on your shoulder, looks at the brass button on your coat with its one good eye, and settles in like a lodger. Across the quay, a young Lantern of the Watch lowers his lamp, goes the colour of tallow, and fills his lungs. \"THE MAGPIE!\" he bellows, pointing at you with his whole arm. \"Stop -- it's the MAGPIE!\" Every head on the docks turns. The sergeant behind him puts down his pastry.",
